---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import logo from "../../assets/images/logo-gold.png";
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Astral ARRA is a space for exploring the invisible connections between consciousness, time, symbols and human experience."
  activeUrl="/en/about"
>
  <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,52rem)_200px] lg:justify-between lg:gap-16">
    <div class="article-body prose prose-lg prose-arra max-w-none">
      <h1 class="!mb-8 !mt-0 text-5xl md:text-6xl">What is Astral ARRA?</h1>

      <p class="lead-line">
        Astral ARRA is a space for exploring the invisible connections between consciousness, time, symbols and
        human experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        Here I gather my observations from an ongoing process of inquiry – synchronicities, esotericism,
        mythology, astrology, Human Design and other systems of knowledge. I don’t see them as separate
        disciplines, but as interconnected languages through which we can explore reality and our own existence.
      </p>

      <h2>Synchromysticism</h2>
      <p>
        Synchromysticism is a concept I am developing as a way to explore the meeting points of synchronicity,
        mystical experience and a non-linear perception of time. It treats signs, coincidences and recurring
        symbols not as isolated events, but as possible pieces of a larger system of connections between the inner
        world and outer reality. At its heart is the experience of the Beyond-reality – a space where timelines,
        symbols, intuition and personal consciousness interweave in ways that challenge our usual understanding of
        cause and sequence. Synchromysticism is at once a philosophical framework, a research approach and a
        personal practice of observing, documenting and interpreting these phenomena.
      </p>
      <p class="lead-line">
        Astral ARRA is a reflection of my own path – a place where experience meets knowledge and curiosity turns
        into research.
      </p>

      <h2>About me</h2>
      <p>
        For years I have been studying astrology, esoteric traditions and the symbolic systems through which
        humanity has tried to understand the link between the visible and the invisible world.
      </p>
      <p>
        My interest in religions and mythologies led me to many cultures and ancient civilisations, with a special
        focus on Islam, Sumer and Ancient Egypt. Learning Arabic and Hebrew added another dimension to this – language
        as a carrier of symbols, meanings and layers of knowledge.
      </p>
      <p class="lead-line">
        Philosophy gave me the questions, the ancient traditions the starting points, and personal experience the
        direction.
      </p>
      <p>
        Later, Human Design appeared on my path. It became one more tool for exploring human nature and helped me
        connect concepts I had until then been looking at through different systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over time my interest reached beyond the established frameworks. I began to explore synchronicities, the
        non-linear perception of time, consciousness and the interplay between different levels of reality.
      </p>
      <p>
        I don’t see the search for knowledge as something that is ever finished. To me it is movement –
        observing, comparing, experiencing and rediscovering.
      </p>
      <p class="closing-line">The journey never ends. It only reveals new directions.</p>

      <div class="not-prose mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-4">
        <a href="/en/portal" class="border-b border-neon pb-1 text-ice-100 hover:text-neon">Enter the portal</a>
        <a href="/en/blog" class="border-b border-gold/60 pb-1 text-pearl-muted hover:border-gold hover:text-gold-300">
          Read the articles
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Image
      src={logo}
      alt=""
      widths={[200, 400]}
      sizes="200px"
      class="sticky top-10 hidden w-[200px] self-start opacity-90 lg:block"
    />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Key sentences set apart in the display face, aligned left rather than justified */
  .article-body .lead-line,
  .article-body .closing-line {
    font-family: theme("fontFamily.display");
    text-align: left;
    hyphens: manual;
    color: theme("colors.ice.100");
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .article-body .closing-line {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: theme("colors.gold.300");
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .article-body .lead-line,
    .article-body .closing-line {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
